  data:  # 11b6
    kind: invariant  # 11b6
    title: "First-party hypergumbo_* symbols emitted as external_symbol path=<external>"  # 11b6
    status: violated  # 11b6
    priority: 2  # 11b6
    parent:  # 11b6
    tags:  # 11b6
    - dogfooding  # 11b6
    - pass12  # 11b6
    - classification_axes  # 11b6
    - medium_severity  # 11b6
    isbefore: []  # 11b6
    duplicate_of: []  # 11b6
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 11b6
    pr_ref:  # 11b6
    description: ""  # 11b6
    fields:  # 11b6
      statement: "366 'imports' edges target external_symbol nodes whose canonical_name starts with python:hypergumbo_ (i.e., first-party workspace packages). The behavior map has 331 unique such nodes including __version__, parse_tier_spec, fold_array_join, scip_pb2.Index, etc. All have path=<external> and supply_chain tiers internal_dep (hypergumbo_core.*) or external_dep (hypergumbo_tracker.*). The actual function/class definitions exist as separate proper nodes — so the import is mis-routed to a phantom external twin instead of being resolved to the real first-party node. Special sub-case: 3 of these are ORPHANS (no inbound edges) and correspond to pyproject.toml [project.scripts] entries (hypergumbo_core.cli:main, hypergumbo_tracker.cli:main, hypergumbo_tracker.cli:textconv_main); the console-script declaration creates the external node but no edge references it."  # 11b6
      root_cause: "The Python analyzer's import-resolution stage doesn't traverse the workspace-sibling package map (packages/*/pyproject.toml) to recognize hypergumbo_* as first-party. Combined with HHH (tier classifier same gap) and KKK (stdlib catalog gap), 22% of Python externals are recoverable. Pyproject.toml console-script parsing is similarly siloed — it creates external_symbol nodes without linking to the in-tree definitions."  # 11b6
- op: discuss  # 7815
  at: '2026-05-28T21:07:22Z'  # 7815
  by: agent  # 7815
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7815
  clock: 2  # 7815
  nonce: '7815'  # 7815
  message: "Pass 13 root-cause refinement: tier asymmetry confirmed empirically. Tier counts on first-party hypergumbo_* externals: hypergumbo_core (154), hypergumbo_lang_common (40), hypergumbo_lang_extended1 (56), hypergumbo_lang_mainstream (52), hypergumbo_lang_rust_analyzer (2) ALL get supply_chain.tier_name='internal_dep' with reason='direct dependency (pyproject.toml)'. hypergumbo_tracker (27) gets supply_chain.tier_name='external_dep' with reason='unresolved external reference'. Root cause: the tier classifier reads the ROOT pyproject.toml dependency list (which names hypergumbo-core, hypergumbo-lang-*, but NOT hypergumbo-tracker). It does NOT scan workspace member pyproject.tomls. Fix: enumerate packages/*/pyproject.toml and treat all workspace members as internal_dep (or better, first_party once PPP's symbol-emission half is fixed)."  # 7815
